import Yt.X509.Cert
/-! The trust anchors compiled into the app: only the roots that the app's
hosts chain to. Determined on 2026-11-01 with `openssl s_client -showcerts`
against www.youtube.com, i.ytimg.com and redirector.googlevideo.com
(TLS 1.3): all three serve `leaf <- WE2 <- GTS Root R4` when ECDSA is
offered and `leaf <- WR2 <- GTS Root R1` when only RSA signature schemes
are offered (each chain also carries a GlobalSign Root CA cross-sign of the
GTS root, which path building does not need).

DER from https://pki.goog/repo/certs/gtsr{1,4}.der; SHA-256 fingerprints
checked against the macOS system root store and webpki-roots 1.0.11 (the
roots the Rust client used). -/
namespace Yt.X509.Roots
open Yt.Crypto

